   "slot": "member1_opening",
   "text": "A collateral price crash fits LUSD's liquidation mechanism because the Stability Pool absorbs debt from troves that fall below their maintenance requirement, and any remaining shortfall is redistributed pro rata to surviving troves rather than sold. This process means no forced sale exists on the absorption path, so the system does not rely on selling collateral against exit liquidity to cover losses.\n\nThe headline results show that collateral coverage remains at 3.25 before and after the shock, with zero bad debt and zero collateral that must be sold. The exit liquidity available in this scenario is $8.8M, and the ratio of forced sales to exit liquidity is zero because no sales occur.\n\nLUSD that can be redeemed against troves before the redemption fee reaches its ceiling is not counted because the crash path is excluded from the calculation. The Stability Pool balance available to absorb liquidations in this scenario is $6.6M, which reflects the pool balance less the share of liquidity providers leaving.",
   "think": false,
